01. EC2 + ALB:
This is one of the most common real-world architectures.

                  Internet
                     |
                  Route 53
                     |
                    ALB
                 /       \
                /         \
             EC2-1       EC2-2

ALB distributes requests.

If:
EC2-1 → unhealthy

ALB can stop routing traffic to that target.


02. EC2 + Auto Scaling:
This is where EC2 becomes truly useful for DevOps.

Imagine:

Normal traffic:

EC2-1
EC2-2

Traffic increases:

EC2-1
EC2-2
EC2-3
EC2-4

Traffic decreases:

EC2-1
EC2-2

Auto Scaling manages this based on configured policies.



03. Launch Template

Launch Template defines how new EC2 instances should be created.

It can specify:

AMI
Instance type
Security groups
IAM role
User data
EBS
Network configuration

Then:

Launch Template
       ↓
Auto Scaling Group
       ↓
EC2 instances

This is an extremely important DevOps concept.



04. Auto Scaling Group:
ASG manages a group of EC2 instances.

Example:

Minimum = 2
Desired = 2
Maximum = 6

Normal:

EC2-1
EC2-2

High traffic:

EC2-1
EC2-2
EC2-3
EC2-4
EC2-5

After traffic decreases:

EC2-1
EC2-2



05. Self-Healing

This is a major DevOps use case.

Suppose:

EC2-1
EC2-2

EC2-1 crashes.

ASG detects the unhealthy instance:

EC2-1
  ↓
Unhealthy
  ↓
Terminate
  ↓
Launch replacement
  ↓
EC2-3

This is called self-healing infrastructure.
